 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-6", "title": "UNVERIFIED: serve's browser folder-upload arm was not exercised end-to-end (form markup, field name 'files', and the zip path all verified; needs a desktop browser or a multipart test to close)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-20 (dogfood run, serve surface, real Chromium via CDP).\nEVIDENCE: GET / -> the form has two inputs: <input type=file id=folder name=files webkitdirectory multiple> and <input type=file id=zipfile name=zip accept=.zip>. serve accepts BOTH field names (verified: POST -F 'zip=@two-boards.zip' -> HTTP 200, 3 boards; POST -F 'bogusfield=@two-boards.zip' -> HTTP 200 + '0 boards found in upload' notice). The folder arm is the README's FIRST documented path ('pick a board folder') and the only one that does not require the user to build a zip by hand.\nWHAT I COULD NOT DO: drive the folder upload as a user. A 'folder picker' input requires the browser to attach a real directory from a real file chooser - there is no scriptable path that a headless/CDP session can use, and I will not fake a pass. I verified the form markup, the field name the handler expects (serve.go:327 files=append(files, fps...)), and that no input other than 'files'/'zip' is named in the form.\nTHIS ROW IS THEREFORE A FALSIFIABLE CLAIM, NOT A PROVEN DEFECT: state plainly that the folder-upload arm was NOT exercised end-to-end in this run. Either (a) someone with a desktop browser confirms a folder upload end-to-end and this row closes as verified-working, or (b) the arm is found broken and fixed. A third, more useful outcome: add a regression test that posts a multipart request with relative-path file parts (the shape webkitdirectory sends) and asserts the boards register - that would convert this from an unverifiable manual step into a gated one.\nACCEPTANCE: the folder path is either demonstrated working from a real browser or covered by an automated multipart test; the row does not close on 'the markup 