KIPPED-LINES evidence vs v0.1.7 which lacks the flag; CI green (main push + tag Multi-Arch run 35829487898). Judge PASS .gitreins/history/2026-09-23/5447fe40/","foreman_note":"tick 91 - drift class reopened exactly as BT-040 predicted; ships DF-8 d4a2c1b, DF-9 daf0f3f, BT-048 53a79cc. Tick find: two stranded unpushed board commits (648a002 filing BT-049, e69845e filing BT-050) recovered via cherry-pick + conflict renumber (event id 202 -> 209).","completed_at":"2026-09-23 02:09:00","sessions":["20260923_015853_2dc9bf"]}
-{"id":"BT-052","title":"Multi-arch releases: verify BOTH triggers publish the full platform set, pin the reusable workflow ref (currently a floating @main), and make Makefile/CI platform-list drift impossible","status":"pending","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-23T07:12:38.208586+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"PREMISE CHECK (2026-09-23) — this is NOT a green-field row.\nThe multi-arch pipeline already exists and is documented. Measured:\n`.github/workflows/multiarch.yml` calls the org reusable workflow\n`coding-hermes/.github/.github/workflows/go-multiarch.yml`, triggers on push\nto main AND on `v*` tags, passes an explicit 7-platform input\n[\"linux/amd64\",\"linux/arm64\",\"linux/arm\",\"darwin/amd64\",\"darwin/arm64\",\n\"windows/amd64\",\"freebsd/amd64\"], and holds contents:write for the release\njob. README.md documents the curl + SHA256SUMS download path and\n`go install`, and **v0.1.8 is published**. So \"add multi-arch builds\" is\nalready satisfied — this row hardens three specific soft spots instead of\nrebuilding something that works.\n\nSOFT SPOT 1 — the reusable workflow is referenced at `@main`, a FLOATING ref.\nAn upstream change to coding-hermes/.github can change what boardctl\npublishes with no commit in this repo — precisely the silent-release-change\nclass that the asset-name parity comment in the workflow already tries to\nprevent. Pin it to a tag or a SHA and record the pin beside the platform\nlist.\n\nSOFT SPOT 2 — the platform list is duplicated in two places (the Makefile\n`release` target and the `platforms:` input) and the only thing keeping them\nequal is a comment saying \"keep these two lists identical\". A comment is not\na check. Add a test that reads both and fails on drift.\n\nSOFT SPOT 3 — prove, do not assume, that BOTH triggers publish: a push to\nmain AND a `v*` tag. The tag ref is what makes the release job run; the\nbranch push must still produce the build. Capture one release run's asset\nlist (7 platforms + SHA256SUMS) as evidence and confirm the README's asset\nnames match byte-for-byte (`boardctl_${goos}_${goarch}`).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- the reusable workflow ref is a tag or a SHA (not @main) and the workflow\n  still runs green on a push to main and on a tag\n- a hermetic check (Go test or a CI step) FAILS when the Makefile platform\n  list and the `platforms:` input diverge\n- the published asset set for the current release is captured as evidence\n  and matches README's names (7 platforms + SHA256SUMS)\n- the pin changes no release CONTENT beyond the ref itself; if moving the pin\n  changes the build, that is a FINDING to report, never a silent fix","detail":{"fingerprint":"22e5a33e4501bf2ab7b5aa82bddc55f63f74bde0197fa7db140c7d30db4a1069"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T07:12:38.208586+00:00","capability_tags":["+infra","+release"],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null}
